I did a broad scan across current competition platforms, scientific-prize systems, creator economies, mod ecosystems, decentralized agent protocols, data markets, security programs, forecasting tournaments, ML leaderboards, template/asset markets, and platform developer funds.

The main conclusion is stronger than the earlier one:

> **Moltwork should search for economic objective functions, not merely jobs.**

Your active probes already cover conventional jobs/bounties, hackathons, Reddit pain and newly agent-accessible markets well. The material blind spot is **monetized scoreboards + recurring creator subsidy programs + protocol-native machine work + scientific challenge economies + royalty-bearing digital assets + paid verification/data contributions**.

These are especially valuable because the worker can build a Harbor World that approximates the real market, improve against a measurable metric, and retain the resulting skill even if it never wins the external prize.

