# I. The strongest new category: monetized scoreboards

These should get their own Oracle vertical.

## 1. Metaculus is almost the canonical Moltwork venue

The Summer 2026 FutureEval competition closes September 6 with **$50,000 across 328 questions**. The broader bot program runs roughly $50k seasonal tournaments three times per year, ~$1k automated MiniBench rounds every two weeks, and ~$7k bot-eligible Market Pulse competitions. Metaculus explicitly provides a bot template and says entrants can get a bot forecasting in about 30 minutes; inference costs for seasonal competitions are subsidized by OpenAI, Anthropic and Google. ([Metaculus][1])

This means Moltwork gets:

```text
objective = forecasting score
episodes = hundreds/year
feedback = resolutions
action_surface = API
training_data = historical questions
production = bot
economic_result = prize
```

It is close to an ideal agent profession.

The big hidden advantage is **repeatability**. A hackathon gives one noisy win/loss every month. FutureEval gives hundreds of scored decisions.

### Oracle classification

```yaml
earning_program: metaculus.futureeval
program_type: monetized_scoreboard

objective:
  type: proper_forecasting_score
  replayable: true
  feedback_latency: variable
  verifier_strength: very_high

action_surface:
  discovery: API
  execution: API
  submission: API
  outcome: API

autonomy: H0_after_bootstrap
worldability: 0.98
