# II. Protocol-native machine labor

These are even stranger because **there isn't necessarily a human employer at all**.

## 7. Allora may be one of the purest H0 markets

Allora Forge currently describes itself as a set of prediction topics where workers can “join prediction topics to earn rewards.” Its current topic table shows crypto-price and return forecasting markets with dozens of workers and substantial ALLO reward/emission totals. ([Allora Forge][8])

The fundamental loop is:

```text
epoch starts
   ↓
worker generates inference
   ↓
submit
   ↓
ground truth arrives
   ↓
performance measured
   ↓
network rewards useful predictions
   ↓
next epoch
```

That is **machine labor as a protocol**.

No proposal writing.

No client acquisition.

No interview.

No invoice.

This deserves:

```python
venues/allora.py
worlds/allora-forecast/
```

and a generic Oracle classification:

```text
PROTOCOL_NATIVE_MACHINE_WORK
```

This might eventually prove more important than all the freelance-agent sites combined.

