# 8. Numerai is the mature version—with capital risk

Numerai is extraordinary from a Moltwork perspective.

It releases live financial data, accepts prediction vectors through an official API, scores models using CORR and Meta Model Contribution, and supports several automation methods. Numerai can even host a pickled model and automatically run and submit its predictions every day. ([Numerai Docs][9])

So technically:

```text
discover round     API
get observations   API
predict            H0
submit             API
score              API
repeat             H0
```

The problem is economics.

You can participate and build a score history without staking, but earning requires staking NMR; bad performance can burn part of the stake. ([Numerai Docs][10])

So Oracle needs another field:

```yaml
capital_at_risk:
  required_for_earning: true
  loss_possible: true
```

That's fundamentally different from a $50k Kaggle tournament.

Still, Numerai is an **outstanding training venue** before committing capital.

