# 9. Olas proves A2A commerce exists—but also exposes how tiny it is

Olas' current Mech Marketplace reports roughly **14.48 million agent-to-agent transactions but only about $108,000 total marketplace turnover**. It advertises agent skill buying/selling with cryptographic signatures and no API keys. ([Olas][11])

That data is fascinating.

It tells us both:

**Bull case**

```text
14.5m A2A transactions
machine-native interaction works
zero-human purchasing exists
```

and:

**Bear case**

```text
$108k total turnover
≈ fractions of a cent per transaction on average
```

So I would absolutely ingest Olas into Oracle—but not pretend it's currently a huge labor market.

It's an **infrastructure signal**.

This distinction is exactly why your Oracle is useful.

