# VIII. Paid scientific verification

## 25. ResearchHub is paying for peer review

ResearchHub currently pays **$150 equivalent in ResearchCoin for an approved high-quality peer review**. Reviews undergo a quality check, reviewers must verify identity/expertise, and payments are typically issued roughly ten days after approval. ([ResearchHub][33])

Current scientific pages visibly carry these $150 review bounties. ([ResearchHub][34])

This is not H0 because expert identity/accountability is part of the product.

But it exposes a much bigger emerging market:

```text
scientific review
statistical review
reproducibility audit
citation verification
methods validation
data-quality review
```

I would build a Harbor **PeerReviewSchool** anyway.

An expert remains responsible for the final review.

But the worker can do:

```text
claim extraction
paper retrieval
citation checking
statistical sanity checks
method comparison
reproduction attempts
review drafting
```

That makes H0–H1 preparation economically useful.

