# 30. Steam Workshop economies

Steam's Workshop infrastructure can allocate revenue from sold items to individual Workshop authors, and Steam handles author banking, tax and payouts on supported implementations. ([Steamworks][41])

Crucially, this isn't one market.

It's:

```text
game × workshop monetization model
```

So the Oracle adapter should discover individual games where:

```text
UGC accepted
creator payout enabled
current demand
content technologically generatable
```

The weird niche might not be “Steam Workshop.”

It might be:

> one relatively obscure game whose paid item ecosystem is suddenly growing.

That's exactly the Yu-Gi-Oh-style discovery problem.

